# What graphify must never read — including when it is told to ignore
# .gitignore.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS WHEN .gitignore ALREADY LISTS ALL OF IT. graphify reads
# .gitignore and then this file by default, and with `--no-gitignore` it reads
# THIS FILE ALONE (graphify/detect.py, the per-directory loader). So the one
# flag that would walk the licensed export into a knowledge graph is exactly
# the case in which .gitignore stops counting. Listing the corpus here is what
# keeps it out under that flag too. tests/verify-leakguard.js holds this file
# to leak-guard's own list, so the two cannot drift apart.

# The licensed corpus, and every directory made of it — the same four that
# scripts/leak-guard.js refuses by path (rule 1, DIRS).
source/
build/
content/
dist/

# graphify's own output, and the run log whose lines quote question text
# (leak-guard's DERIVED and FILES).
graphify-out/
tests/last-run.log

# Vendored and minified. Its single-letter names (u, p, h, r, s, l) collide
# with real functions of the same names in src/core/heart3d.js, and graphify
# resolves by name — so it fabricated edges between the two files, supplied
# five of the ten "god nodes" in a report, and headed that report's suggested
# questions with "why does u() connect heart3d.js to lottie.min.js?". It does
# not; nothing here is anyone's code to read.
assets/splash-heart/lottie.min.js
